<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 23.16 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 23.16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 83 basis points to 23.16 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     22.83	    23.16		   +83 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.98	    23.37		   +39 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.99	    23.31		   +32 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.94	    24.10		   +16 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
